{
  "summary": "This experiment tested an RNA-only baseline using PCA encoding (pca_n2000) without image data or fusion, establishing a single-modality benchmark. Validation accuracy of 0.4849 (F1: 0.4639) suggests performance lower than the existing multimodal configuration (0.5266 accuracy). Uncertainty remains about whether multimodal integration provides incremental value, as the RNA-only baseline lacks direct comparison with other single-modality approaches."
}

